    <span class="blog-tag">Technology &amp; AI</span>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.35rem,3.5vw,1.9rem);font-weight:800;line-height:1.25;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:.5rem;">How AI Is Changing the 2026 FIFA World Cup Forever</h1>
    <p class="article-meta">July 2026 · 9 min read · <a href="/blog/" style="color:var(--accent);">ZippyWidgets Blog</a></p>

    <div class="card article-body">

      <p>The <strong>2026 FIFA World Cup</strong> is officially the largest live deployment of artificial intelligence in sports history. Spanning 104 matches across the United States, Canada, and Mexico, the expanded 48-team tournament has pushed AI from experimental luxury into the operational core of football — changing how goals are given, how tactics are planned, and how billions of fans experience every match.</p>

      <p>Driven by a headline technology partnership with Lenovo, machine learning is now embedded into the match ball, the broadcast feed, the coaching bench, and the stadium infrastructure. This article breaks down exactly what has changed, how the technology works, and what it means for the game — both now and in the next World Cup cycle.</p>

      <h2>1. The Trionda Match Ball: AI at 500 Readings Per Second</h2>

